  "invariants": [
    "Native monitoring check, usage, proposal observation and notification projection share one SQLite transaction",
    "Semantic risk dedup ignores check time and preserves read state while advancing the source reference",
    "Quiet hours use named time zones and actual UTC minutes including DST; no OS delivery",
    "Every list, count, open and read mutation rechecks actor, login generation, window, frame, database and canonical source",
    "No Goal objective, task or memory body is copied to notification projections or renderer localStorage",
    "Host invalidation and Pinia synchronous auth subscription fence same-user relogin and late list/read/open results",
    "Navigation uses a freshly authorized minimal target and focused Goal reread, never a cached reference as authority"
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Engineering fixtures with real SQLite and isolated packed public entry closure; trusted test storage opener is not a production ACL claim",
    "Vue components run in Happy DOM; Electron/window/dialog, IPC and router boundaries are simulated, not a real Electron GUI journey",
    "Prepared workspace lacks UI dependencies; renderer uses isolated Temp vue-router/ant-design-vue/icons dependencies and a Happy DOM resolver, without modifying repository dependencies or lockfiles",
    "Delivered authorized notifications describe historical checks; paused, ended, expired or revised Goals do not erase delivered history; pending delivery remains strictly controlled",
    "Only the latest 50 authorized Goal notices are shown; unread badge is scoped to that loaded page",
    "No migration replay of old checks; model output-time memory integration, business effectiveness samples and exact-candidate remote release matrices remain outstanding"
  ]
